Relationships:
-------------
SYSTEM_Controller --> RDG_Module           (initializes geometry + relational basis)
SYSTEM_Controller --> MFE_Module           (initializes flux engine)
SYSTEM_Controller --> Q_Module             (initializes moderation + closure)
SYSTEM_Controller --> RME_Module           (initializes equation)

RDG_Module --> SYSTEM_State                (writes relational geometry)
MFE_Module --> SYSTEM_State                (writes flux dynamics)
Q_Module  --> SYSTEM_State                 (writes moderated slice)
RME_Module --> SYSTEM_State                (writes scoring)

SYSTEM_State --> RDG_Module                (provides geometry for next step)
SYSTEM_State --> MFE_Module                (provides flux for next step)
SYSTEM_State --> Q_Module                  (provides slice for next step)
SYSTEM_State --> RME_Module                (provides full state)

Notes:
------
* SYSTEM_Controller orchestrates the entire relational engine.
* RDG_Module provides geometry (SID Structure, Interaction, Dynamics).
* MFE_Module provides bipolar flux and coupling.
* Q_Module provides moderation, slicing, closure.
* RME_Module provides scoring.
* SYSTEM_State is the unified container that keeps all modules synchronized.
